---
name: pdf-extract-demo
description: PDF text/markdown extraction via the OPT-IN pdf provider
# `std.pdf` lives in an EXPLICIT, OPT-IN provider: build.sbt stages
# v2/runtime/providers/pdf-plugin under bin/lib/providers/pdf and its renderer deps
# (PDFBox, openhtmltopdf, jsoup) "never enter the standard launcher graph". So this case
# runs under `bin/ssc-provider pdf run` and under the v1 interpreter, and CANNOT run under
# `bin/ssc` / emit-js / run-jvm. Measured 2026-07-29: int=ok, js/jvm/v2=fail, and
# `bin/ssc-provider pdf run` renders at rc=0. Declaring the lanes stops the corpus contract
# counting a deliberate packaging boundary as a v2 defect (BUGS v2-optin-provider-cases).
backends: [int]
---

# Pdf extract demo

```scalascript
import std.pdf.*

// Read a PDF's text layer. Here we generate a small document first so the example
// is self-contained; in practice `pdfBase64` is an uploaded / fetched PDF (e.g. a
// PIT-11 tax form) that you want to parse.

val html =
  "<html><body>" +
    "<h1>PIT-11</h1>" +
    "<p>Podatnik: <strong>Jan Kowalski</strong></p>" +
    "<p>Przychod: 84210.00 zl</p>" +
    "</body></html>"

val pdf = htmlToPdfBase64(html)

val pages = pdfPageCount(pdf)
println(s"pages: $pages")                 // pages: 1

val text = pdfToMarkdown(pdf)
println("--- extracted text ---")
println(text)                              // contains "PIT-11", "Jan Kowalski", "84210.00"
```
